sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney> a pk:Claim ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013) & Short et al. (2014) GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 kidney ureteric bud Turing branching morphogenesis faithfully reproduces Mouse embryonic metanephric kidney ureteric bud & cap mesenchyme (Mus musculus, E11.5-E15.5) morphology" ;
        dcterms:description "The simulation script(s) 2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mouse embryonic metanephric kidney ureteric bud & cap mesenchyme (Mus musculus, E11.5-E15.5) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 88.1/100, audit 2026-10-19-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py> ;
        pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py; output: docs/media/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_comparison.png; organism: Mouse embryonic metanephric kidney ureteric bud & cap mesenchyme (Mus musculus, E11.5-E15.5); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/028758bc; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: f9c1a998913eff873333397950c9abd3c6d935d905ec30d2d429a949264e57cf; artifact_sha256: 9f98460186b4bdf7797ab875a51788dba9d5afea8d89977769eda0675a4efdc0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney_reference.json=b624d595c12fdf8d..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg=dceaf5044c7014e4..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/paper_citations.bib=3eb2da09bd233938..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json=8959f600edc5b3b8..., datasets/gdnf_ret_ureteric_kidney/scout_manifest.json=60b78a1876b45c42...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Menshykau & Iber (2013): a ligand-receptor (GDNF-RET) Schnakenberg-type Turing mechanism on the ureteric bud epithelium selects elongation, bifurcation or trifurcation according to the ampulla geometry; GDNF is produced by the cap mesenchyme and bound by epithelial RET | Short et al. (2014): OPT tip counts across E11.5-E15.5 (2 to 354 tips), Horton-Strahler R_b 2.08 and R_L 1.38, stereotyped early branching followed by a spatially regulated nephrogenic-zone programme in which all tips reside beneath the renal capsule | Watanabe & Costantini (2004), Basson et al. (2005), Miyazaki et al. (2000), Shakya et al. (2005): GDNF-bead attraction, Spry1-/- supernumerary budding, BMP4 stalk inhibition and Gdnf-/-/Ret-/- renal agenesis; reconstructed_in_script: 4-species GDNF-RET-Wnt11-Sprouty1 reaction-diffusion solver on a 1D periodic ampulla ring with m = 1..4 mode selection (L212-L361); a 3D stochastic ureteric tree across g = 1..8 with Horton-Strahler ordering (L366-L457, L655-L914); a steady diffuse-domain GDNF field inside an expanding spherical renal capsule with nephrogenic-zone production shell and RET tip sinks (L526-L604) coupled to the tree by chemotaxis, confinement, interstitial dilation and GDNF-gated arrest; a 6-condition capsule coupling sweep (L990-L1051); a 5-condition perturbation suite at g = 5 (L1057-L1101); colour-threshold segmentation of a vendored E12.5 micrograph (L1107-L1215); transfer_boundary: The capsule is a sphere on a fixed Eulerian grid with isotropic dilation, not a moving-mesh finite-element model of the kidney; its radius R_cap(g) is prescribed from the Short (2014) observed tip numbers (L509-L519, L750), so the moving boundary is partly data-driven rather than emergent | Per-generation segment lengths and branch angles are read from the reference table (L743-L747); the tree reproduces the ordering of tip counts, not an independent prediction of the generation-wise geometry | The capsule constants (300/550 um anchors, 110 um nephrogenic zone, 150 um GDNF decay length, kappa_tip 2.0, gate 0.15, chi 0.35) are modelling assumptions tagged as such in renal_capsule_phase_field_reference.json, not literature table values; does_not_claim: A deforming tetrahedral/FEM mesh of capsule and nephrogenic zone, anisotropic tissue growth, an ellipsoidal kidney, epithelial mechanics, cell-level nephron induction, or quantitative reproduction of the specimen micrograph's pErk1/2 fold (the 2.40 reference is unsourced)]" ;
        pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.11.008>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2004.12.004>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.devcel.2014.02.017>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ydbio.2004.09.019>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1088/1478-3975/10/4/046003>,
            <https://doi.org/10.1172/JCI8256> ;
        pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-code-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-model-fidelity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-morphometric-validation>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-overall>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-parameter-expressivity>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-repro-package>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-source-traceability>,
            <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney-specimen-match> ;
        pk:weightOfEvidence "0.881"^^xsd:double .

    <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py> a schema:SoftwareSourceCode ;
        rdfs:label "2014-menshykau-gdnf-ret-ureteric-kidney.py" ;
        schema:codeRepository <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib> ;
        schema:programmingLanguage "Python" ;
        schema:version "028758bc" .
}

